menu "CyberGear CAN example"

    config CYBERGEAR_MOTOR_ID
        int "CyberGear motor CAN ID"
        range 0 255
        default 127
        help
            Target CyberGear motor CAN ID. A factory-default motor normally uses 127 (0x7F).

    config CYBERGEAR_HOST_ID
        int "ESP32 host CAN ID"
        range 0 255
        default 253
        help
            Host CAN ID placed in enable, stop, and feedback frames. The example default is 253 (0xFD).

    config CYBERGEAR_TWAI_TX_GPIO
        int "TWAI TX GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 4

    config CYBERGEAR_TWAI_RX_GPIO
        int "TWAI RX GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 5

    config CYBERGEAR_RUN_LINK_SOAK_TEST
        bool "Run a 60-second zero-effort CAN link soak test"
        default n
        help
            Diagnostic mode for intermittent CAN receive errors. It keeps the measured initial
            position as the target and sends 50 Hz control frames for 60 seconds with desired
            velocity, feed-forward torque, Kp, and Kd all zero. Existing feedback, tracking,
            temperature, and fatal TWAI checks remain active. This mode does not command motion,
            but the motor is enabled during the test and software checks do not replace a physical
            power cutoff. Keep the explicit motion test disabled while collecting a link-soak log.

    config CYBERGEAR_RUN_MOTION_TEST
        bool "Explicitly allow the 360-degree out-and-back test (10 seconds per leg)"
        default n
        help
            WARNING: enabling this option permits physical motor movement. Secure and unload the motor,
            use a current-limited 24 V supply, verify CAN termination, and keep an emergency power cutoff
            within reach. The default build performs communication and zero-effort validation only.
            After 500 ms of zero effort, capture the measured origin, ramp +2pi rad over 10 seconds
            (negative near the positive protocol limit), return over 10 seconds, then stop once.
            Clear the full-turn sweep, prevent cable winding, and supervise the approximately 20-second test.
            Absolute speed must stay below 0.5 rad/s during zero effort and 1.0 rad/s during motion;
            absolute position error relative to the current target must stay below 0.10 rad.
            Abort if position differs from the current trajectory target by 0.10 rad or more.
            Desired velocity follows the signed trajectory slope (+/-0.628 rad/s); feed-forward
            torque remains zero. Kp=90.0 and Kd=1.0 increase effort only when tracking error or
            velocity error appears; they are not hard actual speed or torque limits. Strict
            feedback-torque trips are 1.0 N m during zero effort and 10.0 N m during Motion;
            before each transmission, the combined feed-forward, position-error, and velocity-error
            controller estimate must also remain strictly below the phase's torque threshold.
            These are software checks, not motor current/torque limiters. All thresholds are provisional.

endmenu
